 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Good you' taking care of her. A balanced meal that hits the basic nutrients is easy. A bit of bread, a bit of meat, a bit of peas. Six is old enough to try real food and push boundaries, so don't let her push you too hard. Starter food, like toast and chicken, is actually nice. Stick with it for now. A bowl of grain soup and a slice of toast is food. Let her pour the sauce if you cooking from a box. Lots of little jobs build confidence and make her part of the family.",
